---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import portraitImage from '../assets/images/profile-1.png';
---

<Layout
	title="About Andrew Smith | UX Design Leader & Senior Product Designer"
	description="Andrew Smith — twenty years across product design, front-end development, and UX leadership. Based in Adelaide, South Australia. Available for senior UX and design leadership roles."
>
	<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

	<div class="page">
		<SiteHeader />

		<main id="main-content">
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<div class="hero-layout">
					<div class="hero-copy">
						<h1 class="display-title">Twenty years designing digital products. Still most interested in the problem underneath the interface.</h1>
						<p class="hero-text">
							Senior product designer and UX leader based in Adelaide. I design from research through to shipped product, build the systems that make quality consistent, and lead teams to do the same.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="hero-portrait-wrap">
						<Image
							class="hero-portrait"
							src={portraitImage}
							alt="Portrait of Andrew Smith"
							loading="eager"
							decoding="async"
							widths={[320, 480, 640]}
							sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 32vw"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Background</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Started as a front-end developer — writing HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, building websites and applications for clients across agency, media, and corporate environments. Moved into UX at the University of Adelaide, where I led the shift from traditional web design to a genuine UX practice and built a custom design system used across the whole university.
					</p>
					<p>
						Seven years at RAA after that, first as the senior designer across travel, insurance, member portal, payments, and renewals, then as UX Manager responsible for the team, the practice, and how we deliver. Twenty years of real products, real users, and real engineering constraints.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">How I Work</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Research first. Not as a process step, but because designing without knowing who you are designing for and what they actually need is expensive and usually wrong. I use AI tools to accelerate synthesis, generate journey map structures, and analyse usability data — not to replace the thinking, but to get to the thinking faster.
					</p>
					<p>
						Then design system thinking. Consistent interfaces do not happen because designers are careful. They happen because the decisions are captured somewhere, the components are documented, and the governance exists to maintain them. I have built that infrastructure from scratch twice and know how to make it stick.
					</p>
					<p>
						Then delivery. I work closely with engineers, write clear specifications, and stay involved through build and QA. The design that ships is the one that matters.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Available</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Currently open to senior product designer, UX lead, and design management roles in Adelaide and remotely. <a href="mailto:asmithdigital@gmail.com">asmithdigital@gmail.com</a> or 0400 895 354.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page {
		position: relative;
		width: min(calc(100% - 3rem), 78rem);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.25rem 0 5rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		line-height: 1.4;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero {
		padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
	}

	.hero-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(15rem, 20rem);
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.hero-text,
	.story-block p {
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.hero-text {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait-wrap {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		align-self: start;
		padding-top: 0.35rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait {
		width: min(100%, 20rem);
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.08);
	}

	.editorial-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 2rem;
		padding: 2.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.section-rail {
		align-self: start;
	}

	.story-block {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1100px) {
		.hero-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.75rem;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.hero-copy {
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.hero-text {
			max-width: 42rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait-wrap {
			justify-content: flex-start;
			padding-top: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page {
			width: min(calc(100% - 1.5rem), 78rem);
			padding-top: 1rem;
		}

		.hero {
			padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
		}

		.editorial-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-text,
		.story-block p {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait {
			width: min(100%, 16rem);
		}
	}
</style>
